        "original_id": "4ff0a916-cb98-5426-9b60-2addff192046",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Foods: meat and three, chicken fried steak, country fried steak\n- Places: Southern United States\n- Concepts: restaurant menus, American cuisine\n\nFacts:\n- In the cuisine of the Southern United States, a meat and three restaurant lets a customer choose one meat from a daily selection of three to six options.\n- In the cuisine of the Southern United States, a meat and three restaurant lets a customer choose three side dishes from a list that may include up to a dozen options.\n- Meat choices at a meat and three restaurant can include fried chicken, country ham, beef, country-fried steak, meatloaf, or pork chop.\n- Side dishes at a meat and three restaurant usually include vegetables, potatoes, corn, and green or lima beans, and can also include gelatin, creamed corn, macaroni and cheese, and spaghetti.\n- Chicken fried steak, also known as country fried steak, is an American breaded cutlet dish.\n- Chicken fried steak consists of a piece of steak, usually tenderized cube steak, coated with seasoned flour and pan-fried.",
